From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terbin <terbin.2b2t@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Gate PaperWorldLoader forceUpgrade on upgradeComplete

Paper's per-world PaperWorldLoader.loadWorldData re-invokes
Main.forceUpgrade for each world load. Once minecraft-patch 0014 restored
the up-front call in Main.main, this duplicates work and on
--recreateRegionFiles spams "Failed to replace an old region file"
errors because new_region/ was already moved away by the first pass.
Skip the per-world invocation when ArchiveSettings.upgradeComplete is set
(i.e. when Main.main already ran the upgrade).

diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/PaperWorldLoader.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/PaperWorldLoader.java
index 66ee5e01f18946d30ff322b3d8a4eb93677a7373..d82db618b275e8dff00eee9c86fa7baae9ebc9ba 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/PaperWorldLoader.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/world/PaperWorldLoader.java
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ public record PaperWorldLoader(MinecraftServer server, String levelId) {
             primaryLevelData.setModdedInfo(this.server.getServerModName(), this.server.getModdedStatus().shouldReportAsModified());
         }
 
-        if (this.server.options.has("forceUpgrade")) {
+        if (this.server.options.has("forceUpgrade") && !archive.ArchiveSettings.upgradeComplete()) { // The Archive - skip when Main.main already ran the upgrade
             Main.forceUpgrade(this.server.storageSource, DataFixers.getDataFixer(), this.server.options.has("eraseCache"), () -> true, this.server.registryAccess(), this.server.options.has("recreateRegionFiles"));
         }
 
